    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8208": {
      "title": "Open Rank Social Work Faculty",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Open Rank Social Work Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Open Rank Social Work Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Open Rank Social Work Faculty Position Number 977523 Department Social Work & Sociology Salary $60,000-$95,000 Remote No Job Summary Angelo State University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Social Work. The successful candidate will teach courses in the B.S.W., M.S.W., and/or D.S.W. programs; engage students in research and professional development; and contribute to the continued growth and accreditation of the Social Work programs. The anticipated start date is January 19, 2027. Essential Duties Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Social Work. Maintain an active program of scholarly or professional activity. Advise and mentor students and support their professional development. Involve undergraduate and graduate students in research, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Support program development, assessment, and compliance with CSWE accreditation standards. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of current Social Work practices and CSWE accreditation standards. Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Ability to conduct research and engage students in scholarly activities. Ability to contribute to program development, assessment, and continuous improvement. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and university leadership Minimum Qualifications MSW degree from a CSWE -accredited social work program with two years post graduate experience; Doctorate in social work or related field for Assistant Professor applicants. ABD / ABC candidates will be considered if the degree can be completed within the first year of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Professional licensure or eligibility for licensure. Experience with CSWE accreditation. Experience with program development in an academic or non-academic setting. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F393P Open Date 10/16/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 01/19/2027 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of References Transcripts (Unofficial) Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at 