    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8179": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Artificial Intelligence Position Number 977278, 977301 Department Computer Science Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experience Remote No Job Summary The Department of Computer Science at Angelo State University invites applications for the full-time, nine-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Artificial Intelligence, beginning in August 2027. The successful candidate will support undergraduate and graduate programs in Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science and contribute to the interdisciplinary mission of the university’s AI Center of Excellence through teaching, research, student mentoring, curriculum development, and engagement with external partners. Applications are encouraged from candidates across a broad range of artificial intelligence areas, including technical, applied, and human-centered AI. Relevant areas may include machine learning, generative AI, natural language processing, computer vision, robotics, autonomous systems, edge and embedded AI, AI hardware and systems, human-AI collaboration, AI literacy and education, responsible AI, and interdisciplinary applications of AI. The faculty member will normally teach three courses per semester, maintain an active research agenda, pursue external funding, mentor students, and collaborate across disciplines on AI-related research and educational initiatives. The academic appointment, tenure home, and formal evaluation pathway are within the Department of Computer Science. Essential Duties Teach three undergraduate and/or graduate courses per semester in artificial intelligence, computer science, data science, computer engineering, or related areas, as assigned by the Department Chair. Develop and continuously improve courses, laboratories, assignments, and other instructional materials supporting Artificial Intelligence and Computer Science programs, and collaborate on interdisciplinary AI curriculum development. Maintain an active research and scholarly agenda in artificial intelligence or an AI-related interdisciplinary field, including technical, applied, or human-centered AI. Develop and submit proposals for external funding and participate in externally funded research, educational, or workforce-development initiatives. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research, capstone projects, applied AI projects, professional development, and career preparation. Contribute to the interdisciplinary mission of the AI Center of Excellence through collaboration across colleges and departments on AI-related research, educational initiatives, and student projects, including activities that advance AI literacy and responsible AI use. Participate in departmental, college, and university service, including assessment, advising, recruitment, student success, committee work, outreach, and program development. Contribute to developing appropriate partnerships with industry, government, educational institutions, and community organizations to support AI education, research, applied projects, and workforce development. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Knowledge of artificial intelligence concepts, methods, systems, and applications, with depth in one or more technical, applied, or human-centered areas. Knowledge of current and emerging developments in artificial intelligence and their relevance to academic disciplines, professional practice, and workforce needs. Knowledge of effective teaching practices, student-learning assessment, curriculum development, and instructional technology. Knowledge of research methods and scholarly practices appropriate to the candidate’s area of expertise, including scholarly publication, grant development, and externally funded projects. Knowledge of interdisciplinary approaches to AI research, education, and integration, including AI literacy and human-AI collaboration. Knowledge of ethical, secure, responsible, and transparent uses of artificial intelligence, including privacy, bias, reliability, and societal impact. Skills Effective teaching and student-engagement skills at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Research, scholarly writing, technical presentation, and grant-development skills appropriate to the candidate’s area of expertise. Skills in developing and improving curricula, courses, laboratories, assignments, and applied AI projects. Effective written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills, including communicating AI concepts to technical and nontechnical audiences. Student mentoring, academic advising, and career-development skills. Collaboration and partnership-development skills across academic disciplines, industry, government, educational institutions, and community organizations. Abilities Ability to teach courses in artificial intelligence, computer science, computer engineering, data science, or related areas. Ability to maintain an active research agenda and produce scholarly contributions appropriate to the candidate’s area of expertise. Ability to mentor students in research, capstone experiences, applied AI projects, and professional development. Ability to teach effectively in face-to-face, online, or hybrid formats as assigned. Ability to collaborate across colleges and departments on AI-related research, curriculum development, and educational initiatives. Ability to contribute to the AI Center of Excellence through interdisciplinary projects, AI literacy activities, and engagement with external partners. Ability to adapt teaching and research activities in response to evolving technologies and workforce needs. Ability to contribute effectively to departmental, college, university, professional, and community service. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Data Science, or a closely related field from an accredited institution or international equivalent. ABD candidates will be considered, provided the doctorate is completed no later than September 1, 2027. Academic preparation and expertise appropriate for teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related areas. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective university-level teaching and student mentoring. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, an active research and scholarly agenda in artificial intelligence or an AI-related interdisciplinary field, including technical, applied, or human-centered AI. Ability to collaborate across disciplines and contribute to the instructional, research, and service missions of the Department of Computer Science, the AI Center of Excellence, and the university. Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements No physical requirements. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F385P Open Date 09/09/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/02/2027 Review Start Date 11/06/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8134": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants interested in being considered for an interview should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, statement describing their research and/or creative practice, contact information for three professional references, and examples of professional and student work. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Position Number 977225 Department Visual and Performing Arts Salary $53,500 Remote No Job Summary The Angelo State University College of Arts and Humanities and Department of Visual and Performing Arts invites applications from qualified candidates to teach online and face-to-face courses in Video Game Art and Animation. The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Video Game Art and Animation is a new degree within the Department of Visual and Performing Arts. The ideal candidate will be able to help shape this degree for the next generation of video game artists. Applications will be accepted continuously and reviewed as instructional needs develop. Ideal candidates will demonstrate strong abilities in art, creativity, design, and technology, supported by professional or academic experience in game design, technical art, real-time production, and game development processes. They should be capable of integrating visual arts with technology and teaching students how visual design, 3D modeling and asset creation, animation, lighting, materials, shaders, optimization, and interactive features function together in professional game-production settings. They will also mentor students with backgrounds in graphic design, digital art, and traditional fine arts. The goal is to help students transfer their existing artistic knowledge into game development and build industry-focused technical art portfolios that demonstrate professional-level skills. Essential Duties Teaching: Instruct undergraduate studio art courses ranging from foundation drawing and design to courses involving Real-Time, Level Dressing, VFX for games, 2D Animation, 3D Modeling and Sculpting, Lighting, Rendering and Look Development. Other art courses as assigned. Research and Creative Works: Maintain a significant, ongoing studio practice with a record of professional accomplishments, such as solo and group exhibitions at local, regional, national or international levels. Professional Service: Serve on departmental and university committees. Manage studio facilities and assist in the coordination of the Video Game Art and Animation program. Participate in student recruitment and retention. Participate in departmental and Art Area meetings and events. Maintain regular office hours. Work collaboratively and productively with faculty colleagues to meet the needs of the student body. Curriculum Development: Lead or collaborate on revisions of the curriculum, integrating traditional skills with conceptual and interdisciplinary practices. Create curriculum for new courses within the VGAA curriculum to include both online and face-to-face modalities. Mentorship: Academic advising and mentoring BFA art students. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Proficiency in 2D and 3D digital art tools used in contemporary game and animation production. Proficiency in 3D asset creation and integration, procedural production techniques, lighting, materials, shaders, rigging, animation systems, artist-oriented scripting, AI-supported creative workflows, XR optimization, and other commonly used tools and processes associated with game development and real-time production. Ability to recruit, retain students in the Video Game Art and Animation concentration. Participate in departmental/Art Area meetings and events. Maintain regular office hours. Work collaboratively and productively with faculty colleagues to meet the needs of students and the Art Program. Minimum Qualifications An MFA or PhD in game design, game programming, or a closely related discipline, including fields such as computer science, computer programming, or interactive design. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience within the game industry is highly desirable. At least two years of hands-on experience in game development using Unreal Engine production methods. Strong technical proficiency with Unreal Engine, Microsoft Visual Studio, C++, C#, Python, JavaScript, HLSL / GLSL , Verse, Advanced Blueprint Visual Scripting, computer graphics math, performance profiling, and specialized pipelines like Niagara VFX , animation and rendering. Familiarity with industry-standard software, tools, and production workflows, including Autodesk Maya, Mudbox, Adobe Substance 3D, Adobe Creative Cloud, Blender, and ZBrush. Physical Requirements Standing/sitting, bending, lifting, carrying as necessary per the job duties. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F388P Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 01/19/2027 Review Start Date 10/19/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants interested in being considered for an interview should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, statement describing their research and/or creative practice, contact information for three professional references, and examples of professional and student work. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Other Optional Documents 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8133": {
      "title": "Instructor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Instructor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Instructor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor of Art, Video Game Art and Animation Position Number 977232 Department Visual and Performing Arts Salary $43,175 Remote Will be considered Job Summary The Angelo State University College of Arts and Humanities and Department of Visual and Performing Arts invites applications from qualified candidates to teach online and face-to-face courses in Video Game Art and Animation. The Bachelor of Fine Arts in Video Game Art and Animation is a new degree within the Department of Visual and Performing Arts. The ideal candidate will be able to help shape this degree for the next generation of video game artists. Applications will be accepted continuously and reviewed as instructional needs develop. Ideal candidates will demonstrate strong abilities in art, creativity, design, and technology, supported by professional or academic experience in game design, technical art, real-time production, and game development processes. They should be capable of integrating visual arts with technology and teaching students how visual design, 3D modeling and asset creation, animation, lighting, materials, shaders, optimization, and interactive features function together in professional game-production settings. They will also mentor students with backgrounds in graphic design, digital art, and traditional fine arts. The goal is to help students transfer their existing artistic knowledge into game development and build industry-focused technical art portfolios that demonstrate professional-level skills. Essential Duties Teaching: Instruct undergraduate studio art courses ranging from foundation drawing and design to courses involving Real-Time, Level Dressing, VFX for games, 2D Animation, 3D Modeling and Sculpting, Lighting, Rendering and Look Development, particularly in the online modality. Create curriculum for new courses within theVGAAcurriculum to include both online and face-to-face modalities. Other art courses as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Proficiency in 2D and 3D digital art tools used in contemporary game and animation production. Proficiency in 3D asset creation and integration, procedural production techniques, lighting, materials, shaders, rigging, animation systems, artist-oriented scripting, AI-supported creative workflows, XR optimization, and other commonly used tools and processes associated with game development and real-time production. Ability to recruit, retain students in the Video Game Art and Animation concentration. Participate in departmental/Art Area meetings and events. Maintain regular office hours. Work collaboratively and productively with faculty colleagues to meet the needs of students and the Art Program. Minimum Qualifications An MFA or PhD in game design, game programming, or a closely related discipline, including fields such as computer science, computer programming, or interactive design. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience within the game industry is highly desirable. At least two years of hands-on experience in game development using Unreal Engine production methods. Strong technical proficiency with Unreal Engine, Microsoft Visual Studio, C++, C#, Python, JavaScript, HLSL / GLSL , Verse, Advanced Blueprint Visual Scripting, computer graphics math, performance profiling, and specialized pipelines like Niagara VFX , animation and rendering. Familiarity with industry-standard software, tools, and production workflows, including Autodesk Maya, Mudbox, Adobe Substance 3D, Adobe Creative Cloud, Blender, and ZBrush. Physical Requirements Standing/sitting, bending, lifting, carrying as necessary per the job duties. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F389P Open Date 09/18/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8100": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of English",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of English Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of English Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants for the position should submit a cover letter, CV, transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of English Position Number 998687 Department English & Modern Languages Salary $53,500 Remote No Job Summary The Angelo State University Natalie Zan Ryan Department of English and Modern Languages is seeking a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English, specializing either in pre-Civil War American literature or post-World War II American literature. The position also includes teaching core curriculum courses in writing and literature, advanced undergraduate courses, and graduate courses for the online English MA program. The successful candidate will be broadly trained in American literature beyond their research specialization. Essential Duties The dedicated educator and scholar will teach a range of courses across the English curriculum, including: First-Year Composition Sophomore-level American Literature Upper-division undergraduate English courses Online graduate-level English courses The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities include: Engaging in scholarly research and publishing in the candidate’s area of specialization Advising and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students Participating actively in departmental, university, and community service Contributing to curriculum development and program enhancement Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge English composition and American literature. Current trends, research, and scholarship in English studies and the candidate’s area of specialization. Skills Teaching first-year composition and literature courses. Instructional design and curriculum development for undergraduate and graduate courses, including online delivery. Written and verbal communication. Organization, time management, and prioritization. Abilities Design and deliver engaging instruction across undergraduate and graduate levels, including online formats. Mentor and advise students effectively. Collaborate professionally with colleagues and participate in academic governance. Contribute to departmental, university, and community service initiatives. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in English or a closely related field ( ABD considered with expected completion by start date) Evidence of effective teaching at the college level A record of or potential for scholarly publication Preferred Qualifications Experience with online instruction is preferred Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F383P Open Date 09/08/2026 Close Date 12/15/2026 Desired Start Date 08/23/2027 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants for the position should submit a cover letter, CV, transcripts, and three letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately. Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
