    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7840": {
      "title": "Instructor of Exercise Science",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Instructor of Exercise Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Instructor of Exercise Science Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor of Exercise Science Position Number 998290 Department Kinesiology Salary $45,000 - $50,000 Remote No Job Summary The Department of Kinesiology invites applications for an Instructor of Exercise Science position. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate courses in Exercise Science and related areas. Primary teaching responsibilities include Foundations of Kinesiology, Principles of Wellness, Exercise Testing and Prescription, Strength and Conditioning Theory, and Internship/Practicum supervision. The position also includes student advising, service to the department and university, and active engagement in student success initiatives. Essential Duties Teach undergraduate courses in Exercise Science and Kinesiology, including: Foundations of Kinesiology Principles of Wellness Exercise Testing and Prescription Strength and Conditioning Theory and Practice Other courses as assigned based on departmental needs Supervise and evaluate Exercise Science internship and practicum experiences Advise and mentor undergraduate students regarding academic progress, career development, and professional preparation Assist students in obtaining internship placements and experiential learning opportunities Participate in departmental assessment, curriculum development, and accreditation-related activities Serve on department, college, and university committees as assigned Support student recruitment, retention, and engagement initiatives Participate in community outreach and professional development activities Maintain office hours and actively engage in student success efforts Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching Ability to effectively teach exercise science concepts in both classroom and laboratory settings Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills Ability to build positive relationships with students, faculty, internship supervisors, and community partners Demonstrated ability to mentor and advise students Experience utilizing instructional technology and learning management systems Ability to develop and deliver courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment Strong organizational and time-management skills Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, Strength and Conditioning, or a closely related field from an accredited institution Evidence of successful teaching or instructional experience Demonstrated knowledge of exercise testing, exercise prescription, and strength and conditioning principles Be in good standing with the NSCA with a current CSCS certification Ability to supervise and evaluate student internships and experiential learning opportunities Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail 