    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7808": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor of Anatomy &amp; Physiology",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Clinical Instructor of Anatomy &amp; Physiology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Clinical Instructor of Anatomy & Physiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Clinical Instructor of Anatomy & Physiology Position Number 997109 Department Health Science Professions Salary $50,000 Remote No Job Summary The Department of Health Science Professions at Angelo State University in San Angelo, Texas is seeking applicants for a non-tenure-eligible Clinical Instructor position to teach Anatomy and Physiology. Candidates must have prior college teaching experience and a minimum of 18 graduate hours in Biological Sciences or Anatomy and Physiology–related coursework; specific discipline is open. The selected candidate will collaborate with faculty on course instruction, curriculum development, and laboratory activities. Essential Duties Teaching is the primary responsibility for this position, along with additional service and departmental duties as assigned. This is a nine-month appointment with the possibility of teaching summer courses. The role requires flexibility to teach morning, afternoon, and evening courses and labs. The selected candidate will teach undergraduate courses in Health Science Professions for both majors and non-majors, with a focus on human anatomy and physiology. Responsibilities include collaborating with faculty on course design, curriculum development, and laboratory activities. The position also involves participation in departmental, college, and university initiatives, as well as advising students and serving on committees. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities The successful applicant will demonstrate strong written and verbal communication skills, along with excellent interpersonal and organizational abilities. A commitment to creating engaging and effective learning experiences is essential. Candidates should show a strong dedication to excellence in teaching and service, with a commitment to maintaining high professional standards in all settings. A solid foundation in anatomy and physiology is required to effectively teach and assess rigorous undergraduate-level courses. The position requires strong instructional skills and the ability to work collaboratively with colleagues in a professional and collegial environment. Engagement in community service and ongoing professional development is encouraged. Minimum Qualifications Earned M.S. in Biological Sciences or related field from an accredited institution with college-level teaching experience Preferred Qualifications Physical Requirements Must be able to prep and utilize technology related to the assigned courses. EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F375P Open Date 06/15/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher 