    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/7676": {
      "title": "Instructor of Commercial Aviation / Air Traffic Operations",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Instructor of Commercial Aviation / Air Traffic Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Instructor of Commercial Aviation / Air Traffic Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor of Commercial Aviation / Air Traffic Operations Position Number 977248 Department Management & Marketing Salary $75,000 Remote No Job Summary The successful candidate for this position will teach air traffic operations ( ATO ) courses within the Commercial Aviation program. This position will start in August 2026. Essential Duties The individual hired for this position will be required to fully participate in the activities of the CAV Program to include teaching, recruitment, student advising and service on committees. The teaching assignments for this position will cover Air Traffic Operations (Air Traffic Control). Administrative assignments include (but aren’t limited to) playing an active role in helping to set up the Air Traffic Operations track in the CAV program and recruiting students into the program. The successful candidate may also assist in getting the ATO track certified for special designations from the FAA . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Candidates should have a record of successful teaching. Candidates are expected to hold the required FAA certificates to teach air traffic control courses. Minimum Qualifications Masters degree in a field related to aviation. FAA certificates to teach air traffic control courses. Excellent written and oral English communication skills Willingness to support the CAV program through student recruitment and advising and administrative tasks as decribed above. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the college or university level. A background in aviation or aviation instruction. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F370P Open Date 04/23/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 08/17/2026 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (Unofficial) List of References Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
