    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8228": {
      "title": "Instructor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Instructor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Instructor of Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Instructor of Mathematics Position Number 999439 Department Mathematics Salary $45,000 Remote No Job Summary The Department of Mathematics at Angelo State University invites applications for an Instructor of Mathematics with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. We seek a dedicated educator who is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student success. The successful candidate will teach developmental mathematics, core curriculum mathematics, and other lower-division mathematics courses, primarily at the precalculus level and below. The department values effective teaching, meaningful faculty-student interaction, and a commitment to helping students develop mathematical understanding and confidence. This position offers the opportunity to work in a collegial academic environment where quality instruction and individual attention to students are central to the department’s mission. Essential Duties The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and student engagement. Responsibilities include: Teaching 30 semester credit hours of mathematics courses each academic year Developing and delivering effective instruction in developmental mathematics, core curriculum mathematics, and other lower-division mathematics courses, with assignments potentially including face-to-face, online, and dual-credit offerings Using appropriate instructional methods and technologies to support student learning Providing academic assistance and guidance to students through office hours and other appropriate means Participating in departmental activities, curriculum improvement, and student success initiatives Contributing to departmental service and outreach activities, with opportunities for additional university or professional service Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Developmental mathematics, core curriculum mathematics, and lower-division undergraduate mathematics curricula Effective instructional practices for teaching mathematics to students with varying levels of preparation Skills Effective teaching of developmental mathematics and lower-division undergraduate mathematics courses Clear written and verbal communication Instructional design and the effective use of educational technology Organization, time management, and collaboration Abilities Design and deliver engaging instruction that promotes mathematical understanding and student success Adapt instructional approaches to meet the needs of students with diverse academic backgrounds Provide effective academic support and guidance to students Collaborate with colleagues and contribute to departmental initiatives Maintain high professional standards and a commitment to continuous improvement in teaching Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Mathematics or a closely related field, or a master’s degree in another field with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours in Mathematics Demonstrated potential for effective mathematics teaching Strong written and verbal communication skills Preferred Qualifications Successful experience teaching mathematics at the secondary or postsecondary level Experience teaching developmental mathematics or supporting students who need additional preparation in mathematics Demonstrated success in developing and teaching online mathematics courses, particularly in accelerated eight-week formats Experience with or interest in teaching online dual-credit mathematics courses Experience using instructional technology and student-centered teaching practices Demonstrated commitment to student success, academic support, and continuous improvement in teaching Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F395P Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 09/01/2027 Review Start Date 01/11/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of References Optional Documents 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8227": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Mathematics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Assistant Professor of Mathematics Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Mathematics Position Number 999342 Department Mathematics Salary $54,570 Remote No Job Summary The Department of Mathematics at Angelo State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mathematics with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. We seek a dedicated educator and scholar who is committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching, scholarly activity, and service. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate mathematics courses, including: Core curriculum mathematics courses Mathematics service courses supporting other academic programs Upper-division mathematics courses for mathematics majors and related programs The department values student-centered teaching, meaningful faculty-student interaction, and scholarly activities that provide opportunities for undergraduate student involvement. The ideal candidate will contribute to student success, curriculum development, and the continued growth of the department’s academic programs. Essential Duties The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities include: Teaching 24 semester credit hours each academic year (18 semester credit hours during the first year of appointment) Developing and delivering effective instruction in undergraduate mathematics courses Engaging in scholarly activities appropriate to the discipline, with opportunities for undergraduate student involvement Advising and mentoring undergraduate students Supporting student success through effective teaching practices and engagement with students Participating actively in departmental, college, university, and professional service Contributing to curriculum development, program improvement, and assessment initiatives Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge Undergraduate mathematics curriculum and effective mathematics teaching practices Current developments in mathematics and the candidate’s area of scholarly specialization Skills Effective teaching of undergraduate mathematics courses at introductory and advanced levels Clear written and verbal communication Instructional design and curriculum development Effective use of instructional technology and appropriate mathematical or computational tools Organization, time management, and collaboration Abilities Design and deliver engaging instruction for students with varied academic backgrounds Support student learning through effective instructional practices and appropriate academic assistance Mentor and advise undergraduate students Maintain an active program of scholarly and professional development Collaborate with colleagues and contribute to departmental and university initiatives Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Mathematics or a closely related field ( ABD candidates considered with expected completion by the appointment start date) Demonstrated potential for effective undergraduate mathematics teaching Evidence of scholarly activity or potential for continued scholarly productivity Strong written and verbal communication skills Preferred Qualifications Successful experience teaching undergraduate mathematics courses Experience with student-centered instructional practices and the effective use of instructional technology Experience with online instruction or dual-credit mathematics courses, or a willingness to teach in these formats Experience involving undergraduate students in research or other scholarly activities Interest or experience in applied mathematics, computational mathematics, data analytics, or interdisciplinary applications Experience in curriculum development, student mentoring, or academic program initiatives Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F396P Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 09/01/2027 Review Start Date 01/11/2027 Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.angelo.edu/postings/8226": {
      "title": "Open Rank Social Work Faculty",
      "description": "Angelo State University Employment Site | Open Rank Social Work Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Employment ASU Homepage Workplace Notices Open Rank Social Work Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Open Rank Social Work Faculty Position Number 999271 Department Social Work & Sociology Salary $60,000-$95,000 Remote No Job Summary Angelo State University invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Social Work. The successful candidate will teach courses in the B.S.W., M.S.W., and/or D.S.W. programs; engage students in research and professional development; and contribute to the continued growth and accreditation of the Social Work programs. The anticipated start date is January 19, 2027. Essential Duties Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Social Work. Maintain an active program of scholarly or professional activity. Advise and mentor students and support their professional development. Involve undergraduate and graduate students in research, as appropriate. Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Support program development, assessment, and compliance with CSWE accreditation standards. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Knowledge of current Social Work practices and CSWE accreditation standards. Ability to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Ability to conduct research and engage students in scholarly activities. Ability to contribute to program development, assessment, and continuous improvement. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and university leadership. Minimum Qualifications MSW degree from a CSWE -accredited social work program with two years post graduate experience; Doctorate in social work or related field for Assistant Professor applicants. ABD / ABC candidates will be considered if the degree can be completed within the first year of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Professional licensure or eligibility for licensure. Experience with CSWE accreditation. Experience with program development in an academic or non-academic setting. Physical Requirements EEO Statement All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or status as a protected veteran. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ), Angelo State University is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to ensure equal access to employment opportunities for qualified individuals with disabilities. We are committed to ensuring that a qualified individual with a disability has the same rights and privileges in employment as non-disabled employees. If an accommodation is requested for the job application process, please contact our office at (325) 942-2168 or email us at hr@angelo.edu . Posting Detail Information Posting Number F392P Open Date 10/26/2026 Close Date Desired Start Date 01/19/2027 Review Start Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Required Number of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? ASU Employment Website Chronicles of Higher Ed HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed Texas Workforce Commission Social Media (LinkedIn. Facebook. Instagram) Employee Referral / Word of Mouth Other Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of References Transcripts (Unofficial) Optional Documents Other 2601 W. Avenue N, San Angelo, Texas 76909 Back to top Copyright © Angelo State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at